    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0273" n="199" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg199"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/564</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 29, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received October 3, 12 noon.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1822. Following is being placarded about the city: <pb facs="0274" n="200"
                        xml:id="pg200"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#center">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">protest meeting</hi>
                        </p>
                        <p>“Free “America wants to execute a Russian emigrant, revolutionist
                                Alexander Berkman. All the soldiers and workers
                            of Petrograd must attend a mass meeting which will be held in Cirque
                            Moderne on Sunday, September 17 [/30] at 7 p.m. to find out how this
                            “free” country deals with its revolutionists. Admittance free.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
